ealth"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes are satisfied. The firewall directly demonstrated throttling while permitting ordinary SSH access, and both behavior and configuration survived a bounded reboot. The mandatory node-restart protocol is strong: it records a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement and connection loss, a changed boot identity, and recovered sshd, firewalld, firewall policy, and SSH behavior; lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["Burst throttling was behaviorally tested over IPv4 only; IPv6 enforcement is shown by active effective rules but was not exercised with an IPv6 burst.","SSH availability was verified through OpenSSH banner exchange rather than a complete authenticated administrative login."]}
